{
  "summary": "The experiment tested an RNA-only model with multiprofile configuration using PCA encoding and average pooling aggregation, isolating the effect of profile setting compared to the singleprofile baseline. Validation accuracy of 0.5907 and F1 of 0.5727 suggest multiprofile may offer better performance than the singleprofile baseline (0.4849 accuracy). Uncertainty remains about the optimal aggregation method and potential benefits of image modality integration, as this configuration excludes image encoders and fusion mechanisms."
}

